cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Jarvis-X in research or technical work, please cite the software and the specific release or commit. For work implementing or discussing the Dr Moagi 3D Ephemeral-Notion Intelligence Framework, preserve the canonical attribution to Matladi Maxwell Moagi (Lord-Xido)."
title: "Jarvis-X"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Moagi
    given-names: Matladi Maxwell
    alias: Lord-Xido
repository-code: "https://github.com/Lord-Xido/Jarvis-X"
url: "https://github.com/Lord-Xido/Jarvis-X"
keywords:
  - deterministic virtual machine
  - bytecode
  - sparse computing
  - geometric autoencoding
  - auditable adaptive systems
  - ephemeral notion intelligence
  - reality-coupled verification
  - Dr Moagi framework
abstract: >-
  Jarvis-X is an experimental deterministic bytecode virtual machine and
  sparse-computing research platform focused on explicit state contracts,
  bounded execution, verifiable provenance, geometric representations and
  carefully constrained adaptive runtime experiments. The repository also
  contains the Dr Moagi 3D Ephemeral-Notion Intelligence Framework, a named
  systems-level synthesis attributed to Matladi Maxwell Moagi (Lord-Xido),
  with canonical provenance recorded at
  docs/attribution/DR_MOAGI_EPHEMERAL_NOTION_FRAMEWORK.md and repository-wide
  inheritance governed by ADR-015.
